WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.061 --> 00:00:04.170
-My next guest is a four-time
Olympic gold-medal gymnast

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:07.240
who's hoping to win even more at
the Tokyo Olympics this summer.

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:09.542
Please welcome Simone Biles!

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:13.145
[ Cheers and applause ]
Simone! Ah! So good to see ya!

00:00:13.145 --> 00:00:15.114
-Thank you, you too.

00:00:15.114 --> 00:00:17.183
-We're gearing up
for the Olympics.

00:00:17.183 --> 00:00:18.751
It's less than 100 days.

00:00:18.751 --> 00:00:21.354
I'm assuming
you're training like mad.

00:00:21.354 --> 00:00:26.493
What is -- For me, training
is putting on gym clothes,

00:00:26.493 --> 00:00:30.330
thinking about it, and then
going, "Ah, I don't have time.

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:31.797
I really have to get to work."
[ Laughter ]

00:00:31.797 --> 00:00:33.733
That's about my training.
-Right, right. I wish.

00:00:33.733 --> 00:00:36.636
-Yeah. Similar schedules?
[ Laughter ]

00:00:36.636 --> 00:00:41.640
-I wish, but, unfortunately,
I train seven hours a day.

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:43.276
I do have Sundays off.

00:00:43.276 --> 00:00:47.479
So, Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday,
Friday, I train twice a day.

00:00:47.479 --> 00:00:51.417
And then Thursday and Saturday,
I train once a day.

00:00:51.417 --> 00:00:54.553
-Now, you normally
have a fun nickname.

00:00:54.553 --> 00:00:57.022
The Final Five, right?
-Yes.

00:00:57.022 --> 00:00:59.726
-But this year, the team
is four people, correct?

00:00:59.726 --> 00:01:01.594
-Right.
-So it can't be Final Five.

00:01:01.594 --> 00:01:02.929
-Yes, it's four.

00:01:02.929 --> 00:01:04.797
We definitely don't know
what we're going to be

00:01:04.797 --> 00:01:07.166
or who is going to be
on the team yet.

00:01:07.166 --> 00:01:11.104
It's always so much fun for
the audience and the fans to try

00:01:11.104 --> 00:01:13.973
to pick or guess the name
that we picked.

00:01:13.973 --> 00:01:17.977
I remember in 2016,
after we made the team,

00:01:17.977 --> 00:01:21.113
we all collectively thought of
a name, and then we announced it

00:01:21.113 --> 00:01:22.315
when we won team gold.

00:01:22.315 --> 00:01:25.285
So that was just our strategy
for that one,

00:01:25.285 --> 00:01:28.921
but it's also fun because fans
get to remember those teams

00:01:28.921 --> 00:01:30.856
that have certain names

00:01:30.856 --> 00:01:33.926
and it's easier for them
to recall who's on which team.

00:01:33.926 --> 00:01:36.462
-I'm wondering can we guess --
We have an audience here.

00:01:36.462 --> 00:01:38.731
I'm trying to predict --
the Fab Four.

00:01:38.731 --> 00:01:39.965
You could do that.

00:01:39.965 --> 00:01:41.400
-Okay, we could do that.
I'll keep it in my pocket.

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:44.804
-Well, I got zero applause,
so let's scratch that.

00:01:44.804 --> 00:01:47.439
Let's scratch that. Wow.

00:01:47.439 --> 00:01:49.909
Didn't expect that response
from the audience.

00:01:49.909 --> 00:01:51.945
Nothing. I got no applause.
Nothing.

00:01:51.945 --> 00:01:54.781
So how about Fantastic Four?

00:01:54.781 --> 00:01:57.650
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Okay. Oh, they like that one.

00:01:57.650 --> 00:02:02.221
-They like that one.
I should maybe stop there.

00:02:02.221 --> 00:02:03.956
Four Door?
[ Laughter ]

00:02:03.956 --> 00:02:05.324
-The Four Door? Okay.

00:02:05.324 --> 00:02:07.693
-Yeah, the Four Door,
because you're gonna slam it.

00:02:07.693 --> 00:02:08.894
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Hey!

00:02:08.894 --> 00:02:10.629
-When you go to the Olympics.
The Four Door.

00:02:10.629 --> 00:02:12.331
Thank you.

00:02:12.331 --> 00:02:14.466
I'm gonna stop there.

00:02:14.466 --> 00:02:16.236
I want to talk to you about
your docuseries.

00:02:16.236 --> 00:02:18.704
Talk to me about this --
"Simone vs. Herself."

00:02:18.704 --> 00:02:20.873
-Mm-hmm.
-What is this all about?

00:02:20.873 --> 00:02:23.276
What are people going to see
when they check this out?

00:02:23.276 --> 00:02:26.479
-Me just taking myself
to new heights in the gym,

00:02:26.479 --> 00:02:30.983
trying new skills, a little bit
of a look inside my life,

00:02:30.983 --> 00:02:33.319
because I feel like people
always think

00:02:33.319 --> 00:02:35.555
I'm always training,
but besides that,

00:02:35.555 --> 00:02:38.558
I have a lot of amazing partners
that I work with.

00:02:38.558 --> 00:02:40.994
So I get to share my time
in between there,

00:02:40.994 --> 00:02:43.162
but it's not all glitz and glam.

00:02:43.162 --> 00:02:45.164
Sometimes we have to get
down and dirty in the gym,

00:02:45.164 --> 00:02:47.366
so it's just a look at my life.

00:02:47.366 --> 00:02:49.302
-You're just a great role model
for --

00:02:49.302 --> 00:02:51.637
-Well, thank you.
-For humans, for everybody.

00:02:51.637 --> 00:02:54.406
But I have two little girls,
and they love you.

00:02:54.406 --> 00:02:58.544
And you are in so many books
that they're reading about,

00:02:58.544 --> 00:03:00.747
so they're flipping out
that you're on the show.

00:03:00.747 --> 00:03:02.181
-Aww.

00:03:02.181 --> 00:03:05.651
-Do you have any, like, words
for -- not my girls.

00:03:05.651 --> 00:03:07.786
I'll ask you for that later.
"Can you leave a message?

00:03:07.786 --> 00:03:08.988
I'm just going to call them
right now."

00:03:08.988 --> 00:03:12.225
[ Laughter ]

00:03:12.225 --> 00:03:15.461
What is your message
to young women out there?

00:03:15.461 --> 00:03:17.029
-Yeah, of course.

00:03:17.029 --> 00:03:20.132
I would definitely say it
doesn't matter where you start.

00:03:20.132 --> 00:03:22.802
It's where you are going and how
you pick yourself back up

00:03:22.802 --> 00:03:25.204
from those falls,
and just dream big

00:03:25.204 --> 00:03:26.839
and then dream bigger
after that,

00:03:26.839 --> 00:03:29.442
'cause you never know where
your dream will take you.

00:03:29.442 --> 00:03:30.976
-I love that!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:30.976 --> 00:03:32.778
Dream big, dream bigger.

00:03:32.778 --> 00:03:34.147
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:03:34.147 --> 00:03:37.616
Here is Simone Biles
in the Facebook Watch docuseries

00:03:37.616 --> 00:03:39.919
"Simone vs. Herself."
Take a look.

00:03:39.919 --> 00:03:44.123
-I'm, like walking in, like two
minutes before practice starts.

00:03:44.123 --> 00:03:45.591
I'm like, "Who am I?

00:03:45.591 --> 00:03:46.959
This is so unlike me,

00:03:46.959 --> 00:03:49.262
but I seriously just can't get
up anymore."

00:03:49.262 --> 00:03:52.598
-Next break.
-It's a very different change.

00:03:52.598 --> 00:03:54.867
But I still go in there
and get my work done.

00:03:57.036 --> 00:03:59.772
-She does what she has to
be doing in training.

00:03:59.772 --> 00:04:01.407
She will be very, very fit.

00:04:01.407 --> 00:04:02.909
There is no issue with that.

00:04:02.909 --> 00:04:04.243
It's the mental.

00:04:04.243 --> 00:04:06.278
She will be
the number-one attraction

00:04:06.278 --> 00:04:08.347
for Team USA over there.

00:04:08.347 --> 00:04:11.350
A lot of pressure
in her shoulders.

00:04:11.350 --> 00:04:15.687
But we're going to try to
take all the pressure away

00:04:15.687 --> 00:04:18.524
from her and just to focus on
what is controllable,

00:04:18.524 --> 00:04:21.027
and it's her own gymnastics.

00:04:21.027 --> 00:04:23.496
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Ooh! Amazing!

00:04:23.496 --> 00:04:25.732
Simone Biles!
-Thank you.

